algorithms.pseudocode:
Input: (X, Gen, step, w)
Output: Matrix A

for x in X:
  for y in X:
    A[x,y] = 0
    for g in Gen:
      if step(g, y, x):
        A[x,y] += exp(w(g))

Complexity: O(|X|^2 * |Gen|)

Input: Equilibrium functional mu, tolerance eps
Output: Partition of X

classes = []
for x in X:
  placed = False
  for cls in classes:
    if |mu[x] - mu[cls[0]]| < eps:
      cls.append(x); placed = True; break
  if not placed:
    classes.append([x])
return classes

Complexity: O(|X|^2)

Phi(Q) = {mu : mu factors through Q}
  = {mu : Q(x,y) => mu(x) = mu(y)}

Psi(F) = intersection of ker(mu) for mu in F
  = {(x,y) : mu(x) = mu(y) for all mu in F}

Galois property: Q <= Psi(F) iff F <= Phi(Q)
